   "lines": [
    "I went in the morning",
    "to see the class races,",
    "which were exceedingly",
    "good; I sat with the",
    "Lees. In the afternoon",
    "I went out to",
    "pass Sunday at",
    "Milton with the",
    "Whitneys, whom I",
    "like very much - espe-",
    "cially jolly Ella[?] and",
    "pretty Miss. Bessie.",
    "We spent the evening",
    "singing, dancing &c."
